[center][size=5][b]Heart of Magic - Black Flame[/b][/size]
[size=3][b]Version 1.0.0 by Iwillbewarlock[/b][/size]
An add-on for Heart of Magic Librarian that adds Saeel's Iron Cage Lantern, turning your own fire spells into a glowing grey-black flame with extra burn damage at a higher Magicka cost.[/center]

[size=4][b]What It Does[/b][/size]
[b]Heart of Magic - Black Flame[/b] (Korean: [b]Heart of Magic - 흑염 달구기[/b]) is an add-on for [b]Heart of Magic Librarian[/b] (by Iwillbewarlock; a rebuild of Heart of Magic - Spell Learning System by Dinkel Zombie).

It adds one wearable item: [b]"Saeel's Iron Cage Lantern"[/b] (Korean: [b]"사엘의 철창 등불"[/b]), worn at the waist (left front of the hip). It is an iron cage with a grey-black flame floating inside, and it gives no light.

While you wear the lantern, you gain the worn effect [b]"Longing"[/b] (Korean: [b]"갈망"[/b]):
[list=1]
[*][b]Grey-Black Fire Visuals:[/b] Your own fire spells look grey-black, including the projectile, the explosion, the casting effect in your hands, the body aura, the fire on targets you hit, and the casting light. "Your fire spells" means ordinary spells that Heart of Magic's spell catalog marks as fire. It is a glowing grey-black flame, not pitch black.
[*][b]Increased Magicka Cost:[/b] Fire spells that have the fire keyword cost 30% more Magicka. A spell that counts as fire only in Heart of Magic's catalog may not get this cost increase.
[*][b]Black Flame Burn Damage:[/b] Your fire hits add [b]"Black Flame"[/b] (Korean: [b]"흑염"[/b]) damage: 2% of the target's maximum Health over 2 seconds, ignoring resistance. Hitting again restarts the 2 seconds; it does not stack. The spell's own damage is still resisted as usual. This does not apply to cloak spells, scrolls, staffs, shouts or powers.
[*][b]Grey Corpse Fire (AE 1.6.1170 and 1.7.104):[/b] On AE 1.6.1170 and 1.7.104 (1.7.104 not tested in game), corpse fire from Frozen Electrocuted Combustion (FEC) also turns grey on enemies killed by your fire while you are wearing the lantern.
[/list]

[b]What is not changed:[/b]
[list]
[*]NPCs' fire spells, a torch you hold, summoned creatures' own fire, and fire traps keep their normal look.
[*]Projectile speed, range and the spells' own damage are unchanged.
[*]Take the lantern off and your fire spells go back to their normal look and cost.
[/list]

[b]How it works:[/b]
When the game starts, the add-on makes private grey copies of the fire visuals from your own load order, vanilla and mods alike, with a small helper program included in the download. Only your own fire spells use the copies; NPCs and other spells keep the original files.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Skyrim Special Edition / Anniversary Edition:[/b] AE 1.6.1170 is the only version tested in game (see the Game Versions section below). Skyrim VR is not supported.
[*][b]SKSE[/b] for your game version.
[*][b]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/b].
[*][b]Heart of Magic Librarian 1.5.0 or newer[/b] (tested with 1.6.0). Black Flame reads the spell catalog Heart of Magic makes when it scans your spells; from 1.5.0 on, Heart of Magic makes it by itself on the first start.
[*][b]Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable 2015-2022 (x64):[/b] The helper program needs it. Most Skyrim setups already have it.
[*][b]Optional - Immersive Equipment Displays (IED):[/b] If installed, IED hangs the lantern at your hip; without IED, the lantern's own worn model is used. With IED you can also move it: add "lanternIedPreset": "frontLeft", "frontRight", "backLeft" or "backRight" to SKSE\Plugins\HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame.json (default frontLeft; restart the game after a change).
[*][b]Disk space:[/b] The generated copies and work files depend on your load order. On the author's test setup (about 4,000 mods) they take about 1 GB in total.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation and First Launch[/b][/size]
[b]Installation:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install the archive with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex.
[*]There is a Korean and an English download. Install only one. They have the same files and FormIDs; only the in-game text differs.
[*]Enable both plugins: [b]HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame.esp[/b] and [b]HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame_Slots.esp[/b].
[*]Keep SKSE\Plugins\HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame.json: without it, the plugin falls back to built-in defaults that differ from the release settings. If it is lost, reinstall the mod.
[*]If you use a loose-file cache mod (such as CRDW), rebuild its cache (Force rebuild) after installing or updating. An old cache will not recognize the new files.
[/list]

[b]First Launch:[/b]
[list]
[*]Start the game and wait at the main menu. The first launch takes longer than usual because the add-on is generating the grey copies. Wait at the main menu before loading a save: this takes about 1-2 minutes on the author's PC (RTX 3070), or longer on a slower PC or larger load order. Nothing on screen shows when it is done; any spells that still look orange after loading will turn grey on the next launch.
[*]If Heart of Magic has no spell catalog yet, its automatic first-start scan makes one first; Black Flame waits for it.
[*]If Heart of Magic's automatic scan is turned off, or you already have a saved tree so it does not scan by itself, run a full scan in Heart of Magic.
[*]If you load a save or start a new game before the catalog is ready, Black Flame does not set itself up for that session. Finish the scan and restart the game.
[*]On AE 1.6.1170, the copies are used right away in the same session. On other game versions, they may only take effect on the next launch, so restart the game once.
[*]With a large load order, some spells may still look orange after the first launch. Restart the game once more.
[*]Later launches reuse the copies that are still valid.
[*]Do not share your generated copies or your catalog with other players. They are made from the files of your own mods.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Finding the Lantern[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]In-game location:[/b] You can find "Saeel's Iron Cage Lantern" (Korean: "사엘의 철창 등불") on a table on the upper level of [b]Ansilvund Burial Chambers[/b] (Korean: [b]안질푼트 매장묘실[/b]), with smoke rising next to it. If you have already visited that location on your current save, the lantern will appear on your next visit.
[*][b]Console commands:[/b] In English, the command [b]help Saeel 4[/b] shows its FormID; then run [b]player.additem <FormID> 1[/b]. Its FormID is [b]FE[/b] + the 3-digit ESL number your mod manager shows for HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame.esp + [b]80D[/b] (example: ESL number FD3 gives FEFD380D). In the Korean version, [b]help 철창 4[/b] works if your console supports Korean input.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Game Versions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]AE 1.6.1170 (Steam)[/b] - [b]Status:[/b] Tested in game. [b]Notes:[/b] Every feature is on. Copies are used in the same session.
[*][b]AE 1.7.104[/b] - [b]Status:[/b] Not tested in game. [b]Notes:[/b] Every feature is on, as on 1.6.1170. The game code these features rely on was read and checked, but this version was never run. Copies are used in the same session when the plugin's checks of the game's file index pass (the same checks as on 1.6.1170); otherwise they take effect on the next launch. This was not confirmed in game, so one restart may still be needed. Scorch marks were checked only on 1.6.1170.
[*][b]Other AE 1.6 and 1.7 versions (incl. GOG 1.6.1179)[/b] - [b]Status:[/b] Not tested. [b]Notes:[/b] Disabled on these versions: the instant aura refresh of spells that give an aura while equipped, the grey FEC corpse fire, the grey Fire Rune glyph, and the instant hand casting effect refresh (your hands update on the next draw or cast instead). Copies may only take effect on the next launch, so restart once if needed.
[*][b]SE 1.5.97[/b] - [b]Status:[/b] Not tested, never run. [b]Notes:[/b] Copies take effect on the next launch (restart once). Disabled on this version: the instant aura refresh of spells that give an aura while equipped, the grey FEC corpse fire, the grey Fire Rune glyph, the grey hand casting effect and its instant refresh, and the grey ground fire and explosions created by the game's own hazard/explosion code.
[*][b]Skyrim VR[/b] - [b]Status:[/b] Not supported.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known Limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The flame is grey-black, not pitch black.
[*]Death flames (an enemy burning to death) stay orange; that is hard-coded in the game engine.
[*]The rune glyph on the ground (Fire Rune) turns grey only on AE 1.6.1170 and 1.7.104 (1.7.104 not tested in game). Scorch marks were checked only on AE 1.6.1170.
[*]The instant aura refresh of spells that give an aura while equipped (such as Fire Storm) when you put the lantern on or take it off works only on AE 1.6.1170 and 1.7.104 (1.7.104 not tested in game).
[*]The FEC corpse fire may stay orange in some cases (for example when your own frost or shock spell hits that corpse afterwards). The grey corpse fire is AE 1.6.1170 and 1.7.104 only (1.7.104 not tested in game).
[*]With the lantern on, if you switch from a fire spell to a non-fire spell that shares the same equipped effect, that spell's light can stay tinted. It is harmless and goes back to normal when you take the lantern off.
[*]Spells that are not in Heart of Magic's catalog keep their normal look, even if they look like fire. An effect shared by a fire spell and a non-fire spell may keep its original look.
[*]A burn effect that started while you wore the lantern stays grey until it ends, even if you take the lantern off.
[*]The inventory preview may not show the flame inside the lantern (the preview does not draw particles). This is normal.
[*]With IED, a follower wearing the lantern does not show it (only the player is set up).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]If you use IED: take the lantern off and save before you remove the mod. Otherwise IED keeps showing the lantern's last state.
[*]Disable and remove the mod. Removing plugins in the middle of a playthrough can leave traces in the save; keep a save from before you installed it.
[*]Delete the generated files:
[list]
[*]In MO2's Overwrite folder (or in the game's Data folder without MO2): [b]meshes\heartofmagic\blackflame\copies[/b] and [b]textures\heartofmagic\blackflame\copies[/b]
[*]The work folder: [b]Documents\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE\HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame[/b] (GOG: [b]Skyrim Special Edition GOG[/b])
[*][b]HoMBF_slots*.json[/b] in your saves folder (with MO2 profile-local saves: that profile's saves folder)
[*][b]HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame.log[/b] and [b]HeartOfMagic_BlackFlame_tester.txt[/b] in the SKSE folder above (logs; attach them to bug reports)
[/list]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Dinkel Zombie[/b] - the original Heart of Magic (Heart of Magic - Spell Learning System).
[*][b]HDharder[/b] - Temp File Framework (GPL-3.0): the add-on uses its findings about the game's file index (function addresses, signatures and data layouts) to make new files visible while the game runs. None of its code is used.
[*][b]SlavicPotato[/b] - Immersive Equipment Displays: its Papyrus API shows the lantern at the hip.
[*][b]GiraPomba[/b] - Lights On - Wearable Lanterns for IED: its IED hip positions are the lantern's position presets.
[*][b]powerofthree[/b] - address references, and Frozen Electrocuted Combustion, whose corpse effects this add-on turns grey.
[*][b]Ershin[/b] - the main-thread hook location also used by Open Animation Replacer, Precision and True Directional Movement.
[*][b]Khajiitistan[/b] - Black Flame (Nexus mod 192777): the colour reference for the look. No files from it are used.
[*][b]The authors of MuIF and KillFeed[/b] - their call offsets for the SE 1.5.97 impact sites.
[*][b]Community Shaders[/b] - its effect shader was the reference for the palette rules.
[*][b]Bethesda[/b] - the grey effect meshes are made from Skyrim's own files.
[*][b]Libraries:[/b] CommonLibSSE-NG (GPL-3.0 with exceptions), nifly (GPL-3.0), DirectXTex, DirectX Tool Kit, DirectXMath, spdlog, {fmt}, JSON for Modern C++ (all MIT).
[/list]

